Game data in js/weather-data.js
  Zone names, weather names and weather percentages are facts and text from the
  FINAL FANTASY XIV game client. They are used under the FINAL FANTASY XIV Materials Usage
  Policy (https://support.na.square-enix.com/rule.php?id=5382&tag=authc), which requires the
  notice above.
  Source: the CSV export of the game tables in xivapi/ffxiv-datamining,
  https://github.com/xivapi/ffxiv-datamining, commit 44948e4cda5846eab0baa9872122a888fcc4f1b1
  (patch 7.57 hotfix 1). That repository publishes no license of its own; only the tables named
  in tools/lib/gamedata.mjs are read, and only the rows for supported zones and nodes are kept.
  Checked against XIVAPI (https://v2.xivapi.com), whose capture is in
  tests/fixtures/xivapi-weather.json.

Game data in js/gathering-data.js
  Item names, places, levels, spawn times and folklore tome names of timed gathering nodes, from
  the same xivapi/ffxiv-datamining commit (GatheringPoint, GatheringPointBase, GatheringItem,
  GatheringPointTransient, GatheringRarePopTimeTable, GatheringSubCategory, ExportedGatheringPoint,
  Map, Item and related tables), under the same Materials Usage Policy. Checked against XIVAPI
  (tests/fixtures/xivapi-gathering.json) and against the node tables on the FFXIV wiki,
  https://ffxiv.consolegameswiki.com, pages "Unspoiled Nodes" (revision 1490944) and
  "Folklore Nodes" (revision 1491386). tests/fixtures/wiki-gathering.json holds only the facts
  read from those revisions (item, zone, times, coordinates, level, stars, tome); no wiki text.

Test vectors in tests/fixtures/weather-vectors.json
  Computed with ffxivweather 1.0.14 (https://github.com/karashiiro/ffxivweather-py, MIT) and
  confirmed with eorzea-weather 3.2.0 (https://github.com/flowercartelet/eorzea-weather, MIT).
  No code from either project is included here.

Icons
  The weather icons and the crystal mark are original to this project. No game images are used.
